# L §5.14 Legs, E §4.2 Holes in the walk, E §9 invariant 1 (tally 2.1.2, issue #31, the user's "refcore wrong, fix after
# S", 2026-11-01): a leg whose place is a hole (dest, no row) books its known side, and every read of the unknown side is
# a hole naming it (a2, a3); results about other places stand (a1: acc_1 is no made-up place, P-9). Invariant 1 leaves
# the leg out, as a leg booked by its ends. a0 = 500.00 - 100.00. tally 2.1.1's refcore counted the hole end as booked
# and refused every ask with ENGINE-INVARIANT (conservation: -100.00 DUK).
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2025-12-31
  start 2025-01-01
  end 2025-12-31

source s "s"
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
input amt: money DUK
input d0: date
input dest: key accounts
place acc_0: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..
place acc_1: accounts DUK lives 2025-01-01..

move mv_0: transfers
  on d0
  leg cash from acc_0 to dest amount amt

ask a0: bal(acc_0, 2025-01-31)
ask a1: bal(acc_1, 2025-01-31)
ask a2: bal(dest, 2025-01-31)
ask a3: mv_0.cash.to

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-01-01
  amt = 100.00 DUK
  d0 = 2025-01-10
  opening[acc_0] = 500.00 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
  opening[acc_1] = 0 DUK at 2025-01-01 start
=== expect
a0: 400.00 DUK
  unfulfilled: mv_0
  cut 2025-12-31
a1: 0.00 DUK
  cut 2025-12-31
a2: ?"dest: no value" (dest)
  cut 2025-12-31
a3: ?"dest: no value" (dest)
  cut 2025-12-31
